  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fruit value chain development Angola</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to present the main findings of the mapping study on the fruit sector in the Lobito Corridor during the incoming trade mission from Angola to the Netherlands, to moderate a workshop with Angolan producers and Dutch stakeholders and to report on potential and possibilities for follow-up.This should result in awareness on the opportunities around the hinterland of the Lobito Corridor for citrus, avocado and mango. Creating mutual understanding of the importance to operate in cluster and synergies with the Dutch private sector. This should lead in the identification of three project leads that are in sync with the for the Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO) and Invest International available instruments. Ideally, this intend by the delegation members to participate should be manifested at the end of the workshop.</narrative>
  </description>
